  "title": "Building Long‑Term Connection",
  "content": "Connection is not built in grand gestures; it is built in small, repeated moments of warmth, presence, and responsiveness. Long‑term connection grows when parents show interest in their child’s world, listen without judgment, and create shared experiences. These moments become the emotional foundation children rely on throughout life.\n\nThis lesson explores how connection can be strengthened through routines, rituals, and daily interactions. Even busy or stressed parents can build strong connection by being intentional with small moments—eye contact, gentle touch, shared laughter, or a few minutes of undivided attention.\n\nParents learn how to create a home environment where connection is part of the rhythm of daily life.",
  "activities": [
    "Create a small daily ritual with your child—such as a bedtime phrase, a morning hug, or a shared snack.",
    "Spend five minutes today doing an activity your child enjoys, letting them lead."
  ],
  "reflectionQuestions": [
    "What moments help you feel most connected to your child?",
    "How does your child show they want connection?",
